<html><head><title>What</title>
<meta http-equiv="content-type" content="text/html; charset=UTF-8"></head><body><div style="margin: 0px; font-family: &quot; font-size: 12px&quot;;"><p style="margin: 16px 0px;"><font color="#000000"><span lang="EN-GB" style="margin: 0px; font-size: 16px; line-height: 30.1167px; font-family: Verdana, Verdana_EmbeddedFont, Verdana_MSFontService, sans-serif;"><span style="margin: 0px;"><span style="font-family: Verdana;">Our society is changing rapidly, </span><span style="font-family: Verdana;">and n</span>ot always for the better. Many of these changes stem from so-called 'wicked problems'—complex issues with no clear solutions. To address these challenges and </span><span style="margin: 0px;">ultimately create</span><span style="margin: 0px;"> a sustainable future, different disciplines and societal actors must collaborate.</span></span><span style="margin: 0px; font-size: 16px; line-height: 30.1167px; font-family: Verdana, Verdana_EmbeddedFont, Verdana_MSFontService, sans-serif;">&nbsp;</span></font></p></div><div style="margin: 0px; font-family: &quot; font-size: 12px&quot;;"><p style="margin: 16px 0px;"><font color="#000000"><span lang="EN-GB" style="margin: 0px; font-size: 16px; line-height: 30.1167px; font-family: Verdana, Verdana_EmbeddedFont, Verdana_MSFontService, sans-serif"><span style="margin: 0px">In a world with such challenges, higher education is not just about getting a job—</span><span style="margin: 0px">it's</span><span style="margin: 0px"> your ticket to </span><span style="margin: 0px">acquiring</span><span style="margin: 0px"> skills for a better and unpredictable future: think leadership, innovation, and problem-solving abilities.</span></span><span style="margin: 0px; font-size: 16px; line-height: 30.1167px; font-family: Verdana, Verdana_EmbeddedFont, Verdana_MSFontService, sans-serif">&nbsp;</span></font></p></div><div style="margin: 0px; font-family: &quot; font-size: 12px&quot;;"><p style="margin: 16px 0px;"><font color="#000000"><span lang="EN-GB" style="margin: 0px; font-size: 16px; line-height: 30.1167px; font-family: Verdana, Verdana_EmbeddedFont, Verdana_MSFontService, sans-serif">Participating in transdisciplinary education gives you the chance to develop new perspectives and insights on existing challenges. It also prepares current and future professionals for a constantly changing world.</span><span style="margin: 0px; font-size: 16px; line-height: 30.1167px; font-family: Verdana, Verdana_EmbeddedFont, Verdana_MSFontService, sans-serif">&nbsp;</span></font></p></div><div style="margin: 0px; font-family: &quot; font-size: 12px&quot;;"><p style="margin: 16px 0px;"><font color="#000000"><span lang="EN-GB" style="margin: 0px; font-size: 16px; line-height: 30.1167px; font-family: Verdana, Verdana_EmbeddedFont, Verdana_MSFontService, sans-serif;">What makes transdisciplinary education even more interesting is that you are not learning alone. The goal is to learn together with your teachers and societal partners—personal development is, after all, a lifelong process. This means that they—teachers and partners—will also learn from you. You have a voice in this process, so use it and dare to speak up.</span><span style="margin: 0px; font-size: 16px; line-height: 30.1167px; font-family: Verdana, Verdana_EmbeddedFont, Verdana_MSFontService, sans-serif;">&nbsp;</span></font></p></div></body></html>